Viz: a root compositor without a window, in software as in headless mode.

An embedder's off-screen view in a process that also has windows has a root
with no window of the system's (no accelerated widget), whose page's frames are
captured from its own frame sink. With GPU compositing such a root already draws
into an off-screen surface (SkiaOutputDeviceOffscreen, for a null surface
handle); in software it asked Ozone for a canvas on window 0, which on X11 is no
window. Draw it in memory there too, as all of them are under --headless.

--- a/components/viz/service/display_embedder/output_surface_provider_impl.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display_embedder/output_surface_provider_impl.cc
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@
 OutputSurfaceProviderImpl::CreateSoftwareOutputDeviceForPlatform(
     gpu::SurfaceHandle surface_handle,
     mojom::DisplayClient* display_client) {
-  if (headless_)
+  if (headless_ || surface_handle == gpu::kNullSurfaceHandle)
     return std::make_unique<SoftwareOutputDevice>();
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
